      "message": "fuzz: allow targets to provide a libFuzzer custom mutator\n\nAdd an optional `mutator` field to FuzzTargetOptions. When the fuzz\nbinary is linked against libFuzzer, LLVMFuzzerCustomMutator dispatches\nto the selected target's mutator, falling back to LLVMFuzzerMutate for\ntargets that don't set one.\n\nCustom mutators can call FuzzDefaultMutate() to apply libFuzzer's\ndefault mutations to parts of the input.\n\nlibFuzzer disables -len_control by default whenever\nLLVMFuzzerCustomMutator is linked in, which would otherwise affect every\ntarget. Targets without a custom mutator get -len_control=100 restored,\nunless it was set explicitly.\n\nWhether the engine provides LLVMFuzzerMutate is detected at configure\ntime, so builds using other engines or the built-in main are unaffected.",
      "committer": {
        "name": "Bruno Garcia",
        "email": "brunoely.gc@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-10-23T19:22:48Z"
      },
